{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "תלכון", :translit "telkhun", :gloss "you shall walk"} {:he "ובמנוסה לא תלכון", :translit "uv'menussah lo telkhun", :gloss "and in flight you shall not walk"} {:he "לא תלכו", :translit "lo telekhu", :gloss "you shall not walk"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["תלכון" "ובמנוסה לא תלכון"]} {:kind :other, :note "Gezeirah shavah linking two forms of תלכון to connect final and first redemption"}], :frame {:text "The second occurrence of תלכון is in Jeremiah 46:28, ובמנוסה לא תלכון, a verse addressed to Jacob promising deliverance. The juxtaposition establishes a gezeirah shavah between the Exodus departure and the promised future redemption, both of which involve Israel not departing empty-handed, as stated at Exodus 3:21–22 and echoed in the promise of future redemption.", :sources ["Jeremiah 46:28" "Exodus 3:21–22"]}} {:quotes [{:he "לא תלכו ריקם", :translit "lo telekhu reikam", :gloss "you shall not go empty"} {:he "לא תלכו אחרי אלהים אחרים", :translit "lo telekhu akharei elohim akherim", :gloss "you shall not go after other gods"} {:he "ביום ההוא נשאתי ידי להם להוציאם מארץ מצרים", :translit "bayom hahu nasati yadi lahem lehotzi'am me'eretz mitzrayim", :gloss "on that day I lifted My hand to them to bring them out of the land of Egypt"} {:he "ואומר אליהם איש שקוצי עיניו השליכו ובגלולי מצרים אל תטמאו", :translit "ve'omar aleihem ish shikutzai einav hashlikhu uvgilulei mitzrayim al titma'u", :gloss "and I said to them, each man cast away the detestable things of his eyes, and with the idols of Egypt do not defile yourselves"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["לא תלכו ריקם" "לא תלכו אחרי אלהים אחרים"]} {:kind :other, :note "Gezeirah shavah on לא תלכו linking the two verses"}], :frame {:text "The warning against idolatry given at the Exodus is described in Ezekiel 20:6–7, where God says He lifted His hand to bring Israel out of Egypt and told them to cast away detestable t